      "graph_node": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.FunctionalInequalities.SemigroupDecay.backward_interpolation_contraction_of_growth",
      "reconstruction": {
        "text": "Let I,I' : ℝ → ℝ be real-valued functions, and let ρ,s,t ∈ ℝ. Assume that I is continuous on ℝ; that for every u ∈ ℝ, I has right-sided derivative I'(u) at u within the ray [u,∞); and that ρI(u) ≤ I'(u) for every u ∈ ℝ. If s ≤ t, then I(s) ≤ I(t) exp(-ρ(t-s)). No sign assumption is imposed on ρ, I, or I'.",
        "text_sha256": "b21c2af46442c3043ba7e5910fe3fbadd97ff01737c6c700e425236081649248",
